{"name":"Half Orc Highlight","hex":"#976f3c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"half","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of two usually roughly equal parts into which anything may be divided, or considered as divided.","One of two equal periods into which a game is divided."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Consisting of a half (½, 50%).","Consisting of some indefinite portion resembling a half; approximately a half, whether more or less; partial; imperfect."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/half"},{"term":"orc","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Orma."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several large, ferocious sea creatures, now especially the killer whale. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orc"},{"term":"highlight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area or a spot in a drawing, painting, or photograph that is strongly illuminated.","An especially significant or interesting detail or event or period of time."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make prominent; emphasize.","To be a highlight of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/highlight"}],"entries":[{"title":"One half","blocks":[{"text":"One half is the multiplicative inverse of 2. It is an irreducible fraction with a numerator of 1 and a denominator of 2. It often appears in mathematical equations, recipes and measurements."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_half","wikidata":"Q2114394"},{"title":"Orc","blocks":[{"text":"An orc is a fictional race of humanoid monsters often found in works of modern fantasy. Originally called \"Goblins,\" the concept of modern orcs can be found in George MacDonald's The Princess and the Goblin, and later adapted into J. R. R. Tolkien's Middle-earth fantasy fiction, where the first uses of the word can be found."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orc","wikidata":"Q19406